WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.798 --> 00:00:03.823
- Sikhism is the world's
fifth largest religion.

00:00:03.823 --> 00:00:06.387
A Sikh's uniform, right,
a beard and turban

00:00:06.387 --> 00:00:07.700
and all the articles of faith,

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.387
when I wear them, I'm
representing equality,

00:00:10.387 --> 00:00:13.541
justice, fairness, and I’m telling the world

00:00:13.541 --> 00:00:15.232
that this is what I stand for and this

00:00:15.232 --> 00:00:17.405
is what I will fight for.

00:00:17.405 --> 00:00:20.122
A Sikh would rather lose his
head than lose his turban.

00:00:20.122 --> 00:00:22.959
I'm Simratpal Singh, I'm
a captain in the US Army,

00:00:22.959 --> 00:00:24.182
and I'm also a Sikh.

00:00:24.182 --> 00:00:26.634
- To attention.

00:00:26.634 --> 00:00:28.325
- May gates.

00:00:28.325 --> 00:00:30.921
- When I found out that I could not serve

00:00:30.921 --> 00:00:33.245
with my articles of faith,
that was a shock to me.

00:00:33.245 --> 00:00:35.615
Sikhs and military
service go hand in hand.

00:00:35.615 --> 00:00:38.120
My great-grandfather served in World War I

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:39.343
for the British Indian Army.

00:00:39.343 --> 00:00:41.305
There is no conflict
between what Sikh values

00:00:41.305 --> 00:00:43.146
are and the army values.

00:00:43.146 --> 00:00:45.485
I started my military career at West Point

00:00:45.485 --> 00:00:46.844
when I was 18.

00:00:46.844 --> 00:00:49.213
I knew I was gonna have
to make a big decision

00:00:49.213 --> 00:00:51.870
of walking away from my articles of faith.

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:54.526
The grooming standards, as far as shaving

00:00:54.526 --> 00:00:57.092
were codified so that
every one of the military

00:00:57.092 --> 00:00:59.703
soldiers looked the same.

00:00:59.703 --> 00:01:01.952
And I was standing in line
right outside the barber shop

00:01:01.952 --> 00:01:04.714
and I’m thinking, ‘well, here it is, right,’

00:01:04.714 --> 00:01:07.853
and I sat down and the ladies

00:01:07.853 --> 00:01:10.223
at the barber shop were surprised.

00:01:10.223 --> 00:01:11.056
I had long hair.

00:01:11.056 --> 00:01:12.683
I had hair all the way to my back.

00:01:12.683 --> 00:01:14.721
I don't know if they
understood what was going on.

00:01:14.721 --> 00:01:16.064
My entire life was changing.

00:01:16.064 --> 00:01:20.033
Everything, my self image,
everything was being shattered.

00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:22.056
And that's when I had to
make a decision, right?

00:01:22.056 --> 00:01:24.154
And the decision I made was I wanna choose

00:01:24.154 --> 00:01:26.267
to serve my country and figure out a way

00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:29.346
to come back to my
articles of faith later on.

00:01:29.346 --> 00:01:32.047
(gentle instrumental music)

00:01:32.047 --> 00:01:35.292
It was after I met the two
gentlemen who were wearing

00:01:35.292 --> 00:01:37.715
their articles of faith
and were in the Army

00:01:37.715 --> 00:01:39.601
that I learned there is a way

00:01:39.601 --> 00:01:42.107
to request religious accommodation.

00:01:42.107 --> 00:01:45.744
I was simply asking for what
I believed were my rights.

00:01:45.744 --> 00:01:47.480
And March 31st was when I received

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:48.748
the permanent accommodation.

00:01:48.748 --> 00:01:52.053
And I had to pause, 10 years later,

00:01:52.053 --> 00:01:54.981
10 years later it had finally happened.

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:57.351
The first day that I wore my uniform

00:01:57.351 --> 00:02:00.934
with my beard and
turban, it was an unreal,

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:03.430
unreal feeling.

00:02:04.475 --> 00:02:05.818
When I look in the mirror now,

00:02:05.818 --> 00:02:09.169
I feel a sense of pride and completeness.

00:02:09.169 --> 00:02:11.070
My two worlds have come together.

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:14.903
(dramatic instrumental music)

